<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/doc-template/templates/page">
<$fill $name="body">

!! Approach

The tiddler is rendered unchanged. A JS widget, `$outline`, wraps the normal body transclusion, walks the rendered widget tree and stamps `data-ol-*` attributes on the DOM node of each unit. One delegated `keydown` and `click` handler lives on the widget's container. Operations are splices of known text ranges. Wrapper elements inside the body are avoided on purpose: they would change the HTML and break CSS such as `ul > li`. The one exception is the widget's own container: while outline mode is on, the whole body sits inside `div.rr-ol-frame > div.rr-ol` (the frame also holds the key overview), so selectors such as `.tc-tiddler-body > p` no longer match (use `.tc-tiddler-body p` or also match `.tc-tiddler-body > .rr-ol-frame > .rr-ol > p`).

!! Parts

|!File |!Role |
|`model.js` |Collects units from the widget tree: start, end, kind, level, parent, siblings |
|`text-utils.js`, `dom-utils.js` |Pure text helpers; DOM lookup shared by widget and editor |
|`formats.js` |Registry of format adapters |
|`block-types.js`, `blocktypes/*` |Registry of block types (tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/rimir/outline/BlockType`, cached in the wiki's global cache until the next tiddler change) and outline's own types as shadows |
|`format-wikitext.js` |Wikitext adapter: indent, promote, move (siblings, and across heading lines), replace, insertNew, insertBlock (after / before / at the end), convert, remove, deleteUnit, merge, split, editSource, isMultiline |
|`outline-widget.js` |The `$outline` widget: unit-to-DOM mapping, stamps, selection, writes |
|`outline-keys.js` |Key dispatch through `$:/config/shortcuts/outline-*`; toggles the key overview |
|`keys/*`, `ui/keys-table`, `keys.tid` |Key groups (caption, hint, list of shortcut names), the overview table, the keys tab |
|`outline-editor.js` |In-place editor: temp tiddler, placeholder, save, continue, conflict handling |
|`outline-menu.js` |Menus at the selection: block menu (Alt-Enter: insert / convert / edit; from the editor: convert only) and delete confirmation (Delete); keyboard and mouse |
|`outline-clipboard.js` |The browser's copy / cut / paste events on the focused outline: the adapter's `copy` gives `{kind, source}`, written as the outline format, as plain text (source) and as HTML (source rendered, tiddler links as text); cut is copy plus `deleteUnit`; paste reads the outline format or plain text (adapter `clipKind`), `paste` parses the clip with the model and rewrites only its item markers / heading levels for the place, one write |
|`outline-undo.js` |Undo/redo: every `writeText` records the text before and after plus the selection in `$:/temp/rimir/outline/undo/<title>`; `undoGroup` makes the save and the operation of a split, merge or editor move one step; undo writes only over the text it left |
|`language/blocks.multids` |Labels of the menu groups and entries (the type labels are the types' captions) |
|`ui/*` |Body template and its filter, help bar (? button and overview), editor template, transclusion marker |
|`styles.tid` |Selection frame and item box, compact editor, marker |

!! Routing

`ui/body-filter` (the first `$:/tags/ViewTemplateBodyFilter` entry; it evaluates the rest of the cascade for the tiddler itself and only takes the body when that ends at the core default, so other plugins' body templates still win, and a filter that yields an empty title for every tiddler, like `else[]`, cannot block it) routes every eligible tiddler to `ui/body` while `$:/config/rimir/outline/enabled` is not `no` and the tiddler has no `outline: no`. `ui/body` renders `<$outline>` around the usual block transclusion, plus the ? button and, while `$:/temp/rimir/outline/help/<title>` is `yes`, the key overview. Both sit outside `<$outline>`, so they never become units; the widget only sets and deletes that temp tiddler (`?`, Escape). The ? button is hidden by CSS until the outline is awake.

!! Idle and awake

The widget renders its children and nothing else until it is woken: no model, no stamps, no `tabindex`, no ResizeObserver; `refresh` only refreshes the children. `wake()` (Ctrl-Click / Cmd-Click on the container, outside links and buttons) adds the class `rr-ol-awake` and `tabindex`, maps the units, starts the observer and a document mousedown listener (capture phase) that calls `sleep()` for a mousedown outside every view of the same tiddler (`ownsTarget`: an `.rr-ol` with the same `data-ol-tiddler`, or the `.rr-ol-frame` around one), so two views of one tiddler do not put each other to sleep. `sleep()` (refused while an editor is open; also Escape with nothing selected) undoes all of it and deletes the selection and help temp tiddlers. A new widget, and an idle one on refresh, wakes itself while the tiddler's selection or edit buffer temp tiddler exists: a re-render keeps an awake outline awake, and another view of the same tiddler wakes with it. When the widget is destroyed in a story river (`tv-story-list`) whose list no longer has its tiddler (close, close all, close others, a changed story list), it discards an open edit and deletes the selection, edit buffer and key overview temp tiddlers, so a reopened tiddler starts idle; a re-render with the tiddler still in the story keeps them. Enter on a transclusion writes a selection on the target's first unit (unless it has one), so the target opens awake. Key, double-click and clipboard handlers return at once while idle. The badge padding column and the ? button only apply to an awake outline.

!! Editor

The editor is a real TW edit widget bound to a temp tiddler (`$:/temp/rimir/outline/...`), placed where the unit was. It lives outside the rendered body's widget tree, so a re-render of the body does not destroy it. Typing changes only the temp tiddler; the real tiddler changes once per save.

The buffer holds the unit's content only: an item's marker and a heading's `!`s (plus the spaces after them), a code block's or `<<<` quote's fence lines, and the first `>` of each line of a whole quote stay in the tiddler and are not part of the edit (`editSource`/`replace` in the adapter). `ui/editor` renders a compact textarea (no toolbar, SimpleEngine) or, with `$:/config/rimir/outline/full-editor` = `yes`, the full text editor with toolbar.

!! Block menu

Alt-Enter in selection mode opens `.rr-ol-menu`, absolutely positioned below the selected unit in `.rr-ol`. Its entries come from the block types (`block-types.js`): //Edit <title>// for each diagram transclusion of the unit (`diagramTargets`), //Add to this item// on a list item (types with the `item` context), //Insert after// / //Insert before// (types with the `block` context; at a list item an item type inserts a sibling, other types go next to the whole list: `insertAnchor`) and //Turn into// (the adapter's `convertTypes`: everything into everything, multi-line content not into one-line types, sub-items and whole lists only between item types, narrowed by the type's `turn-into`). Every adapter function that depends on the types takes them as a last argument (default: the registry of `$tw.wiki`). Insert opens a new-unit editor with a `blockType` (kept in the buffer field `outline-block-type`); saving calls the adapter's `insertBlock`, which puts a new heading after the anchor heading's whole section and any other block right after the heading line (`insertsAfterSubtree`; the editor is placed accordingly). Turn into runs `operate("convert", type)`: a bullet switches its marker character with all its siblings of that level (and their sub-items at that marker position), a whole list at all levels; a heading that changes its level only gets other `!`s (its class stays, its section is not touched); paragraphs, headings and code blocks that change their type are rewritten from their content and set apart by blank lines. `convert` parses its result again and refuses it unless the new unit is where the old one was and the unit count changed only by an added list unit.

Alt-Enter in a new, still empty editor opens the type menu (`retypeMenu`): the editor closes without a write and opens again for the picked type (a typed type with its starter text); Escape reopens it as it was.

Typed blocks: `typedBlockType` recognises a `$$$<content-type>` … `$$$` block of a registered type; `fenced` then gives its header and closing line, so `editSource`, `replace`, Turn into and the badge (`data-ol-type` = the type's badge, `data-ol-typed`) treat it like a code block. An unregistered typed block stays a plain block.

Diagrams: `mapDiagrams` (after stamping, awake only) finds transclude widgets below the body whose target is of a registered typed type, marks their first element with `data-ol-target` (and a transclusion unit itself with `data-ol-diagram`) and records the containing unit; they are no units. `startTargetEdit` opens the editor below that unit on the target's text (or, for //Add to this item//, on the starter text or a template's content), in the tiddler's editor buffer marked `outline-target-mode`; `saveTargetEdit` writes the target, or creates the new tiddler (`newDiagramTitle`) and appends the reference to the item through `writeText` (one undo step). A re-render does not keep such an edit.

Alt-Enter in the editor (`editMenu`) saves first and opens the menu with the //Turn into// entries only (`openMenu({convertOnly, caret})`); the menu keeps `reedit`, so after the conversion, or on Escape, `editAgain` opens the editor on the unit again with the caret where it was.

!! Selection frame

Units get the class `rr-ol-selected`. A list item's element contains its sub-items, so for an item with sub-items the frame is an overlay box (`.rr-ol-selbox`, absolutely positioned in `.rr-ol`) around the item's own lines, measured with a DOM range up to the nested list. It is redrawn on every selection change and when the outline container resizes (ResizeObserver).

A re-render of an ancestor (for example a changed `$:/tags/Global` or `$:/tags/Macro` tiddler re-renders the page template) or closing the tiddler destroys the `$outline` widget. A buffer that differs from what the editor started with is then kept: it carries `outline-orig-source`, `outline-orig-start`, `outline-orig-text`, `outline-is-new` and `outline-unit-kind`, and the next `$outline` widget of the tiddler reopens the editor at the unit, located as on save (or with the conflict notice when the unit is gone). Escape and switching outline mode off discard it.

!! Writes

A single `wiki.addTiddler` of the old tiddler plus the new `text` and modification fields. Before writing, the text must equal the text the positions were computed from, otherwise the view re-renders first. If the text is this view's own last write (a key pressed before the refresh after a write), the operation goes on on the rebuilt mapping; after any other change nothing is written.

Structural operations pass a model guard (`checkOp` in `model.js`) before they are written: the result is parsed again, and a move must keep the unit count and the kinds and levels; indent/promote must keep the unit count and change only the operated subtree's levels, by exactly one. Anything else is refused without a write. Structural keys do nothing while the view has an open editor.

</$fill>
